cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Predicting Cancer Drug Response from Gene Expression:
  disentangling tissue lineage from gene-level signal
message: >-
  If you use this software or its findings, please cite it, and also cite the
  underlying GDSC2 and DepMap datasets listed under references.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Reich
    given-names: Yasmin
repository-code: "https://github.com/yasminreich/Drug-Response-Project"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-24"
abstract: >-
  A leak-free machine-learning pipeline predicting cancer cell-line sensitivity
  to Gemcitabine (LN_IC50) from gene expression, benchmarked against a
  tissue-lineage-only baseline to separate genuine gene-level signal from the
  tissue confound. Compares regularized linear models, tree ensembles, a PyTorch
  MLP, unsupervised autoencoder embeddings and a multi-task network under
  lineage-stratified cross-validation with nested hyperparameter selection, plus
  SHAP-based interpretability. Reports the negative results as well: at p >> n
  with n = 694, no non-linear or deep method outperformed regularized linear
  regression.
keywords:
  - drug response prediction
  - pharmacogenomics
  - gene expression
  - machine learning
  - GDSC
  - DepMap
license: MIT
